### Cars service, port 8102. Works with the REST Client extension for VS Code and with the JetBrains HTTP client.
###
### Start the stack first:  docker compose up -d --wait cars keycloak
### Then run the requests from the top; each one uses what the earlier ones made.
###
### Every request carries api-version. Create and replace use PUT with an id you choose, so a retry is the same
### request: send "If-Match: *" to create, or the ETag you last read to replace that version only.

@host = http://localhost:8102
@keycloak = http://localhost:8080
@version = api-version=2026-11-01

# Ids chosen by the client (UUID v7 in real use; these are fixed so the file can be run again).
@category = 01a16fb5-2222-7000-8000-000000000001
@lisbon = 01a16fb5-2222-7000-8000-000000000002
@porto = 01a16fb5-2222-7000-8000-000000000003

### 1. Sign in as the rental partner (partnerId c0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002 is in the token).
# @name login
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/viatica/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=viatica-cli&username=partner-cars1&password=viatica

@token = {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### 2. The partner's pricing: one flat fee for a one-way rental, a daily surcharge for drivers under 25.
### Before the first save this answers zeros and no ETag; create with If-Match: *.
GET {{host}}/cars/partner/settings?{{version}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
PUT {{host}}/cars/partner/settings?{{version}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: *
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "oneWayFee": { "amount": "25.00", "currency": "EUR" },
  "youngDriverSurchargePerDay": { "amount": "12.00", "currency": "EUR" }
}

### 3. A car category. ACRISS is four letters; minimumDriverAge is the youngest driver it can be rented to.
PUT {{host}}/cars/categories/{{category}}?{{version}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: *
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "acriss": "ECMN",
  "name": "Economy, manual",
  "seats": 5,
  "transmission": "Manual",
  "fuel": "Petrol",
  "bags": 2,
  "minimumDriverAge": 21,
  "imageUrl": "https://images.example/ecmn.png"
}

###
GET {{host}}/cars/categories/{{category}}?{{version}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A category reaches travellers once it is published, and only through the locations of the same partner.
POST {{host}}/cars/categories/{{category}}/publish?{{version}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Two rental locations. Opening hours are one window per weekday, in whole minutes; a missing day is closed.
PUT {{host}}/cars/locations/{{lisbon}}?{{version}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: *
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Lisbon Airport",
  "address": { "line1": "Aeroporto de Lisboa", "city": "Lisbon", "postalCode": "1700-008", "countryCode": "PT" },
  "position": { "latitude": 38.7742, "longitude": -9.1342 },
  "airportCode": "LIS",
  "openingHours": [
    { "day": "Monday", "opens": "08:00:00", "closes": "18:00:00" },
    { "day": "Tuesday", "opens": "08:00:00", "closes": "18:00:00" },
    { "day": "Wednesday", "opens": "08:00:00", "closes": "18:00:00" },
    { "day": "Thursday", "opens": "08:00:00", "closes": "18:00:00" },
    { "day": "Friday", "opens": "08:00:00", "closes": "18:00:00" },
    { "day": "Saturday", "opens": "09:00:00", "closes": "13:00:00" }
  ],
  "cancellationPolicy": { "freeUntilHoursBeforeStart": 48, "penaltyAfter": "FirstDay" }
}

###
PUT {{host}}/cars/locations/{{porto}}?{{version}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: *
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Porto Airport",
  "address": { "line1": "Aeroporto Francisco Sa Carneiro", "city": "Porto", "postalCode": "4470-558", "countryCode": "PT" },
  "position": { "latitude": 41.2481, "longitude": -8.6814 },
  "airportCode": "OPO",
  "openingHours": [
    { "day": "Monday", "opens": "08:00:00", "closes": "18:00:00" },
    { "day": "Tuesday", "opens": "08:00:00", "closes": "18:00:00" },
    { "day": "Wednesday", "opens": "08:00:00", "closes": "18:00:00" }
  ],
  "cancellationPolicy": { "freeUntilHoursBeforeStart": 24, "penaltyAfter": "FullAmount" }
}

### Read it back: the ETag header is the version to send as If-Match when replacing it.
GET {{host}}/cars/locations/{{lisbon}}?{{version}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Your own locations, paged with $top and nextLink. Filter on id, name, status, airportCode, city.
GET {{host}}/cars/locations?{{version}}&$top=10&$filter=status eq 'Draft'&$orderby=name
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Publishing announces the listing on cars.v1 (CarLocationUpdated) and puts it in search.
POST {{host}}/cars/locations/{{lisbon}}/publish?{{version}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
POST {{host}}/cars/locations/{{porto}}/publish?{{version}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Cars and rates: December, five cars a day at 40 EUR, in one request and one transaction.
### Repeatability-Request-ID makes a retry safe: the same id and body gives the first answer back.
POST {{host}}/cars/locations/{{lisbon}}/categories/{{category}}/inventory/bulk?{{version}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Repeatability-Request-ID: 6f1c1b0e-6c0a-4c6e-9d6b-3a5f4f1d0001
Repeatability-First-Sent: Mon, 02 Nov 2026 09:00:00 GMT
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "from": "2026-12-01",
  "to": "2026-12-31",
  "allotment": 5,
  "rate": { "amount": "40.00", "currency": "EUR" }
}

### Weekend rate on one day. The allotment cannot go below what is already sold or held (409 AllotmentBelowCommitments).
POST {{host}}/cars/locations/{{lisbon}}/categories/{{category}}/inventory/bulk?{{version}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "from": "2026-12-12",
  "to": "2026-12-12",
  "allotment": 3,
  "rate": { "amount": "55.00", "currency": "EUR" }
}

### The partner's calendar: allotment, sold, held and the rate for each day.
GET {{host}}/cars/locations/{{lisbon}}/categories/{{category}}/inventory?{{version}}&from=2026-12-07&to=2026-12-14
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. A quote needs no sign-in. Monday 10:00 to Wednesday 10:00 is two rental days. The token pins the price for 15
### minutes; Booking sends it back with the hold request.
POST {{host}}/cars/quotes?{{version}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locationId": "{{lisbon}}",
  "categoryId": "{{category}}",
  "pickUpAt": "2026-12-07T10:00:00+00:00",
  "dropOffAt": "2026-12-09T10:00:00+00:00",
  "driverAge": 35
}

### A young driver pays the partner's daily surcharge (21 to 24 here).
POST {{host}}/cars/quotes?{{version}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locationId": "{{lisbon}}",
  "categoryId": "{{category}}",
  "pickUpAt": "2026-12-07T10:00:00+00:00",
  "dropOffAt": "2026-12-09T10:00:00+00:00",
  "driverAge": 22
}

### One way: drop-off at another location of the same partner adds the partner's flat fee.
POST {{host}}/cars/quotes?{{version}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locationId": "{{lisbon}}",
  "categoryId": "{{category}}",
  "dropOffLocationId": "{{porto}}",
  "pickUpAt": "2026-12-07T10:00:00+00:00",
  "dropOffAt": "2026-12-08T10:00:00+00:00",
  "driverAge": 35
}

### A pick-up outside opening hours is refused (400 LocationClosed, target pickUpAt). Sunday has no hours.
POST {{host}}/cars/quotes?{{version}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locationId": "{{lisbon}}",
  "categoryId": "{{category}}",
  "pickUpAt": "2026-12-13T10:00:00+00:00",
  "dropOffAt": "2026-12-14T10:00:00+00:00",
  "driverAge": 35
}

### 7. The errors a client meets while editing. Without If-Match the answer is 428; with a stale ETag it is 412.
PUT {{host}}/cars/categories/{{category}}?{{version}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "acriss": "ECMN", "name": "Economy", "seats": 5, "transmission": "Manual", "fuel": "Petrol", "bags": 2, "minimumDriverAge": 21 }

###
PUT {{host}}/cars/categories/{{category}}?{{version}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: "1"
Content-Type: application/json

{ "acriss": "ECMN", "name": "Economy", "seats": 5, "transmission": "Manual", "fuel": "Petrol", "bags": 2, "minimumDriverAge": 21 }

### Taking a location off sale announces CarLocationUnpublished. Holds already placed are honoured.
POST {{host}}/cars/locations/{{porto}}/unpublish?{{version}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Holds, commits, releases and cancellations are not HTTP: Booking sends CarHoldRequested, CarHoldCommitRequested,
### CarHoldReleaseRequested and CarBookingCancelRequested on booking.v1, and Cars answers on cars.v1.
